      },
      "rung": "storyline"
    },
    "386": {
      "date": "2026-11-26",
      "edition": "Thursday 26 November",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Fly-half focus",
          "heading": "Fin Smith carried 11 times in 55 minutes of England's All Blacks win",
          "body": "The Northampton fly-half racked up that tally in Saturday's 37-12 win over New Zealand before cramp forced him off. It made him England's third-highest carrier, behind a Ben Earl he called \"greedy\" for his 32 carries. Oval Insights figures have Smith carrying more than any other fly-half in a Six Nations side this year. \"I would hate to be someone that is asking everyone else to go and be physical and put their body on the line, if I wasn't particularly willing to do it,\" he told BBC Sport."
        },
        {
          "kicker": "Around the world",
          "heading": "South Africa's Pieter-Steph du Toit ruled out of France final",
          "body": "Ireland's Dan Sheehan handed two-game suspension. Italy lose Domingo Miotti to thigh injury."
